  "result": "Done — gate verdict **`OK`** (3 of 6 runs used).\n\n**Concept** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/interaction/overtaking.lean`): the body is one leaf per element, in the contract's grouping —\n\n```\nrel_same_direction a b [same_direction_tolerance]\n  ∧ (kin_speed a − kin_speed b ≥ min_speed_excess)\n  ∧ (rel_longitudinal_overlap a b > 0 m  ∨  rel_ahead_behind_in_lane b a)\n```\n\nThe only literal is zero metres (the origin of the signed overlap); both formal parameters are used. One narrowing declared: the overlap is read as *strictly* positive, since the atom is signed and abutting projections are no overlap.\n\n**Witness** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/interaction/overtaking.lean`): two eastbound lanes, two lorries, instance tolerance 0.95 and excess 1 m/s. `holds` is six instants of one whole pass (the overtaking lorry's body over the lane line, centres closing from −13 m to +7 m), `fails` the pair in file at equal speed, `blind` the pass trace with `kin.speed` masked.\n\nGate history:\n1. `VACUOUS` on the in-lane disjunct — with `holds` built as the drawing-level instant alone, that leaf could never decide anything (the overlap disjunct was already true, and `fails` is false on the speed clause whatever it says). I rebuilt `holds` as the whole pass, so the in-lane order carries the clause alone at the first instant and the shared projections alone at the last two.\n2. `WITNESS_FAIL` (`holds` violated, `blind` violated) — the scene, not the body: `Build.scene` derives occupancy from the position only, so the straddling lorry occupied the left lane alone and shared no lane with the other. The pass scene now states the occupancy its footprints cover, which is what `TraceLint.completeOccupancy` derives.\n3. `OK`.\n\nThe record needed no repair. Report written to `/local-scratch2/sma407/scratch_core/launch/remote/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/demo22-1109-0108/iter-001/code/concept__drv_interaction_overtaking/task_result.md`.",
